              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A semi-trailer tire blowout can do more than slow down your day. It can create dangerous driving conditions, damage your trailer, delay deliveries, and lead to expensive downtime that affects your entire operation. For owner-operators and fleet managers, preventing tire issues before they happen is one of the smartest ways to protect both your equipment and your bottom line. Whether you manage a fleet or operate your own truck, staying ahead of tire problems with regular inspections and preventive maintenance can help you avoid costly repairs and unexpected breakdowns.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-causes",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Causes a Semi-Trailer Tire Blowout?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "causes"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-causes-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A semi-trailer tire blowout usually doesn't happen without warning. In many cases, the tire has been showing signs of wear or stress long before failure occurs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-causes-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Some of the most common causes include:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
