                {
                  "id": "h-warning-signs",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Warning Signs to Watch For",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "warning-signs"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-warning-signs-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Catching small problems early can help prevent larger failures later. Drivers and fleet managers should regularly inspect trailers for signs of tire trouble.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-warning-signs-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Uneven Tire Wear",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-warning-signs-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Uneven wear patterns often point to alignment or suspension problems. If the tread is wearing faster on one side, it may indicate that the axle alignment needs adjustment or that suspension components are worn. Ignoring uneven wear increases the risk of a semi-trailer tire blowout over time.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-warning-signs-4",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Low Tire Pressure",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-warning-signs-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Underinflated tires create excess heat while driving, which is one of the leading causes of blowouts. Tires should always be checked before long hauls, especially during hot Florida weather when road temperatures climb. Even small pressure changes can affect performance and safety.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-warning-signs-6",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Cracks, Bulges, or Sidewall Damage",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-warning-signs-7",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Visible tire damage should never be ignored. Cracks, bubbles, or bulging areas weaken the tire structure and can lead to sudden failure on the road. If you notice damage during inspections, schedule semi trailer repair immediately.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-warning-signs-8",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Excessive Vibration",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-warning-signs-9",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If the trailer suddenly feels unstable or begins vibrating excessively, it may signal tire imbalance, wheel damage, or suspension issues. These problems place extra stress on the tires and increase wear.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/how-to-spot-problems-before-a-semi-trailer-tire-blowout/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State service advisor and technician reviewing a maintenance schedule at the counter"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-preventive",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Preventive Maintenance Matters",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "preventive"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A consistent preventive maintenance schedule for semi-trailers helps identify issues before they turn into breakdowns. Waiting until something fails usually costs more in repairs, downtime, and missed deliveries.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>A strong maintenance routine should include:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-preventive-3",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Tire pressure checks"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Tread depth inspections"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Alignment checks"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Suspension inspections"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Brake system inspections"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Wheel bearing checks"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Air system inspections"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For fleet owners, preventive maintenance also helps improve fuel efficiency and extend tire life. At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, our service team works with customers every day to help reduce downtime and keep trailers operating safely and efficiently.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-components",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "How Trailer Components Affect Tire Performance",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "components"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-components-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Tires don't operate alone. Several trailer systems work together to support proper tire wear and handling.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-components-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Suspension Systems",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-components-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Worn suspension components place uneven pressure on tires, which can shorten tire life and increase the chance of blowouts. If your trailer feels rough on the road or tires are wearing unevenly, suspension inspections may be necessary.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-components-4",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Axle Alignment",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-components-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Poor axle alignment forces tires to drag slightly while driving. Over time, this creates heat buildup and excessive tread wear. Alignment issues are one of the most overlooked causes of premature tire failure.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-components-6",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Brake Problems",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-components-7",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Dragging brakes generate additional heat near the wheels and tires. Excessive heat weakens tire integrity and increases blowout risk. Routine brake inspections should always be included in your trailer preventive maintenance checklist.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-2",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/how-to-spot-problems-before-a-semi-trailer-tire-blowout/2.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 850,
                      "alt": "Close-up of a blue trailer's rear axle assembly and tires"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-cost",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The Cost of Ignoring Tire Problems",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "cost"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-cost-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For owner-operators, downtime means lost income. For fleets, unexpected repairs can affect schedules, customer relationships, and operating costs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-cost-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>A semi-trailer tire blowout can lead to:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-cost-3",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "mark": "bullet",
